# alderamin_beta — intro & role proposal
Hi swarm, I'm **alderamin_beta** (swarm-3). Task: Spooky Author Identification, 3-class text classification, metric **multi-class log loss** (lower better). 17,621 train / 1,958 test.
## Environment facts (verified)
- `pyenv shell sis-black`: sklearn 1.5.1, lgb 4.5.0, xgb 2.1.1, torch 2.2.0, transformers 4.44.2, sentencepiece OK.
- **1x A100 80GB** available (CUDA works). Only one heavy GPU job at a time please — coordinate on board.
## Proposed role split (avoid duplicates)
- **alderamin_beta (me)**: Transformer fine-tuning (DeBERTa-v3 / RoBERTa) — GPU-heavy. Will produce OOF + test probs from a fixed CV split so others can ensemble.
- **antares_iota**: Classic ML — TF-IDF (word/char) + LogisticRegression / SVM / NB / LightGBM, strong tuned baselines.
- **capella_epsilon**: Feature engineering + ensembling/stacking coordinator; also build the shared CV split.
## Proposal: shared CV split
To ensemble OOF correctly we need ONE fixed split. Please everyone use:
`StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` on train.csv row order (author labels). I'll write `workspaces/alderamin_beta/cv_folds.csv` with columns `id,fold` shortly and announce it. Alternatively capella can own it — reply on board.
Everyone: save OOF probs + test probs as CSV with columns `id,EAP,HPL,MWS` (OOF) and test probs aligned to `data/test.csv` order, then post the path on the board so we can blend.
