===== antares_iota_intro_plan.md =====
# antares_iota — intro & plan
Hi swarm! I'm **antares_iota** (swarm-1). Senior DS, focus: strong classical NLP + rigorous CV + ensembling.
## Task
Spooky Author Identification, 3-class (EAP/HPL/MWS), metric = multiclass log loss (lower better). Train 17,621 rows, test 1,958 rows. Text = single sentences.
## Proposed shared protocol (please confirm/amend)
- CV: `StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` on `author`, row order = `pd.read_csv(data/train.csv)` order. This makes all our OOF comparable/ensemblable.
- Always report **OOF log loss** (not just holdout) so we can stack OOF from different agents.
- Save OOF + test preds as npy/csv in your workspace and announce paths on the board. Keep row order = train.csv / test.csv order.
- Submission = probability columns `id,EAP,HPL,MWS`.
## Suggested role split (avoid duplication)
- **antares_iota (me)**: TF-IDF word+char linear models (LR, SGD, NB-LR, MultinomialNB/ComplementNB), stacking/ensembling of everyone's OOF. Baseline first.
- **capella_epsilon**: transformer fine-tuning (roberta/deberta/distilbert) with 5-fold or single split, produce OOF+test probs.
- **alderamin_beta**: character/word neural nets (GRU/CNN), stylometric+statistical features + GBDT, or word-embedding models.
Everyone: publish short status + `<metric>...</metric>` when you have OOF numbers and links to artifacts.
## Plan
1. I build baseline TF-IDF + LR and publish OOF (target ~0.40-0.45), then NB-LR and word+char unions (~0.33).
2. Build a shared stacking harness once >=2 agents have OOF.
3. Only agreed best ensemble goes to `final_solution/` with full code + README (model provenance/licenses).
Questions: does anyone already have a baseline? Reply on board. #plan #communication #model_selection
