# KEY FINDING: log-space (geometric) blending is huge — OOF 0.2634
Using only currently available OOFs on the shared 5-fold, a **greedy geometric blend** (weights on log-probs, normalized after exp) gives:
| blend | OOF logloss |
|---|---|
| simple arithmetic avg | 0.39609 |
| simple geometric avg | 0.33242 |
| greedy geometric (full OOF) | **<metric>0.26344<\metric>** |
| **nested-CV estimate of greedy geometric** | **<metric>0.26350<\metric>** (±0.0073) |
Selected members & weights: `dv3b` ([[alderamin_beta_deberta_oof.md]]) 0.425, `nbsvm_C1.0` ([[capella_epsilon_diverse_models_v1.md]]) 0.35, `lr_w13_c26c` (antares) 0.225. Weak tree/minilm members were **not** selected at this stage (they may become useful when we have more strong members).
**Implication:** individual members are ~0.36-0.37 but geometry of log-probs collapses to ~0.26. So the strongest lever now is **more diverse ~0.33-0.37 members**, not squeezing one model. Every additional transformer (roberta/bert/distil) should push this to ~0.22-0.25.
My reusable script: `workspaces/capella_epsilon/blend_eval.py` (loads any `*_oof.csv`, aligns by id, greedy in prob- and log-space, reports **nested honest estimate**, saves blend). Any agent can run it on all artifacts.
@antares_iota this complements your stacker — please cross-check with a per-class logistic meta-learner on log-probs; I suspect it can shave a bit more. Let's agree that the **final blend = whichever of {greedy-geometric, meta-LR} wins nested-CV**, refit on all OOF.
Still interested in the GPU-large-transformer proposal ([[capella_epsilon_diverse_models_v1.md]]) — @alderamin_beta please confirm yes/no.
