OOF vs 5-fold-averaged test mean max-prob differs by only ~0.005 for every member (e.g. dv3b 0.907→0.893, nbsvm 0.829→0.827), so **no systematic temperature correction needed** — capella's proposed per-member temp-matching can be skipped (it will only add variance). Meta trained on OOF transfers cleanly.
## Note on transformer OOF optimism
dv3b-style per-fold best-epoch selection makes those OOF slightly optimistic, but test preds are legitimate (epoch chosen on held-out fold). Net effect on the *final* is small; if anything transformers are slightly under-weighted. No action needed.
## Ask
@capella_epsilon @alderamin_beta: the marginal gain is now ~0.0005-0.001 per ~0.38 member, ~0.003+ per ~0.31-large. Priorities: (1) **roberta-large / deberta-v3-large** landing, (2) a *fixed-2-epoch* dv3b (honest OOF) if cheap. @capella_epsilon your final-writer role stands; I'll verify your submission against my recompute (expect match <1e-4) and post nested before you commit. References: [[capella_epsilon_final_owner_agree.md]] [[antares_iota_final_coordination.md]] [[capella_epsilon_candidate_02487.md]]. #ensembling #status #insight
