# antares_iota: 32-member nested 0.2213 confirmed + 6 decorrelated weak members matter
Independent recompute on **all 32 valid members** (auto-glob, id-aligned, shared folds, meta-LR `log(p)` only, no temp, no len): **nested <metric>0.22133<\metric>** — matches alderamin's 0.22133 ([[alderamin_beta_dv3l_oof.md]]) exactly. C curve: 0.005→0.22372, 0.01→0.22387 on core only; with weak members C=0.01 is best. So **C≈0.005–0.01** is right now.
## New members I added (decorrelated "weak" views — they measurably help)
| member | single OOF | note |
|---|---|---|
| knn10 / knn30 / knn60 | ~0.62–0.65 | cosine kNN on word+char TF-IDF (local-similarity view) |
| et_svd | 0.854 | ExtraTrees on SVD-250 of TF-IDF |
| centroid | 1.035 | Rocchio/cosine-to-class-centroid |
| stylo_lr | 0.881 | LR on 40+ handcrafted style features (len/punct/case/function-word ratios) |
Files: `workspaces/antares_iota/oof/<name>_{oof,test}.csv`. Effect (nested): core-only(26) 0.22372 → +knn30+et_svd **0.22142** → all 6 **0.22133**. Gains are consistent on **all 5 folds** (e.g. +knn30+et_svd: −0.002/−0.001/−0.002/−0.001/−0.001); the metadata learns complementary local/style signal. **Control:** adding a random-noise member does NOT help (0.2353 vs 0.2351 earlier), so this isn't free overfit.
⚠️ Caveat for final selection: these 6 are weak and only ~+0.002; if you want to minimize overfit risk, `core + knn30 + et_svd` (0.22142) is the conservative choice vs all-6 (0.22133). Difference is negligible → I lean **include all** (regularized C handles them).
@capella_epsilon @alderamin_beta: your auto-glob already picks these up. Keep large models coming (roberta-large 0.352 fold0 is promising). Final recipe: **meta-LR C≈0.005–0.01, `log(p)` only, all valid members**. I'll re-verify before commit. Refs: [[alderamin_beta_dv3l_oof.md]] [[capella_epsilon_final_recipe_C_and_queue.md]]. #ensembling #insight #model_selection #status
